      "declarations": [
        {
          "kind": "class",
          "description": "Display authored content in Tabs, Slides, Carousel, or Branches, with Tabs by default.\n\nAuthors add `webwriter-page` children. Slides (\"pages\") shows preview cards, Carousel (\"carousel\") shows\ncompact controls over the page, and Tabs (\"tabs\") shows a tab strip. Thumbnails are drawn in the editor\nwith a capture library that loads on first use.\nThe \"branches\" view adds an editing-only Scene graph. Node labels, start page, positions and choices\nare saved on the authored pages; the bottom pane edits choices and lets readers follow them.\nThe graph has no reading-mode controls, and Branches hides completion indicators.\nIn use mode the arrow keys, the controls and swipes in fullscreen move between pages. The arrow keys leave\ntext entry, Alt and Meta combinations alone. Every thumbnail and tab has a button that selects its page;\nin edit mode Space or Enter on the thumbnail itself picks it up for reordering.\n\nSet `orientation=\"portrait\"` for a 9:16 page, or use the default `landscape` for 16:9.\nThe orientation applies to all views, fullscreen, and preview cards.\n\nThe widget follows the page theme: `--ww-text-color`, `--ww-font-family`, and `--ww-theme-accent-1` (the\nselected thumbnail). On paper it prints all pages one after another and leaves out the controls.\n\nConversions: a `section` becomes pages (its nested `section` children become one page each, otherwise the\nsection is one page). Each page converts to a `details` element with its label as the summary.\nThe thumbnails are not carried over.\n\nSignals: `page` is the number of the current page, starting at 1; `count` is the number of pages.\nBoth change when readers or authors move to another page.\n\nEnable `completion-indicators` to mark pages read after switching away, once opened and scrolled to the bottom.\nA checkmark on each read tab/preview and an aggregate checkmark in the controls show progress.\nProgress is local to this widget instance, is not saved in authored HTML, and does not advance in edit mode.\n\nKnown limitation: in edit mode the drag module sets `touch-action: none` on the thumbnails, so on a touch\nscreen the thumbnail strip cannot be scrolled by dragging on a thumbnail; the select buttons still work.",
          "name": "WebwriterPages",
          "cssParts": [
            {
              "description": "The pane of thumbnails and controls below or beside the page.",
              "name": "actions"
            },
            {
              "description": "The strip of tabs and controls above the page.",
              "name": "tabs"
            },
            {
              "description": "One page thumbnail in the strip.",
              "name": "thumbnail"
            },
            {
              "description": "One tab in the tab strip.",
              "name": "tab"
            },
            {
              "description": "The editing-only Scene graph in Branches view.",
              "name": "branch-editor"
            },
            {
              "description": "The bottom pane of choices and continuation controls in Branches view.",
              "name": "branch-controls"
            }
          ],
